Description: virgl video fixes for VA-API through virgl on AMD (local, not upstream)
 For a Proxmox host (QEMU virtio-gpu-gl, Mesa radeonsi VA) serving guests that use
 Mesa's virgl VA driver; details in https://github.com/fvlaicu/pve-virgl-build
 (docs/DESIGN.md, "The problem"). Needs the guest patch 9999-virgl-guest-video.patch
 (Mesa) for decode readback and scaling.
 .
 1. virgl_video_dma_buf_plane.modifier is 64-bit (was int, truncating DRM modifiers),
    and the EGL dmabuf imports pass it when EGL_EXT_image_dma_buf_import_modifiers
    is there (upstream imports without it, right only for linear surfaces).
 2. Video buffers are exported READ_WRITE. The export is cached per buffer, so a
    decoded buffer fed to the encoder kept its read-only export and the upload was
    refused ("dmabuf is not writable").
 3. glFinish() after a guest frame is copied into the VA surface, before the VA
    encoder reads it through the dmabuf.
 4. H.264 encode: SPS/PPS for each IDR and a slice header for every picture are
    written from the picture description and sent as VAEncPackedHeader buffers.
    Host Mesa >= 24.3 takes the NAL header byte, frame_num, idr_pic_id, POC lsb,
    reference list modifications and marking only from packed headers, and writes
    SPS/PPS into the stream only when it got packed ones; without this every slice
    had NAL header 0x00 and frame_num 0. Level and max_num_ref_frames are chosen
    from frame size, rate and bitrate (the guest sends level 0 and 16 references);
    frame_num/POC lsb lengths are 8 bits, as ffmpeg's. HEVC is not handled.
Author: local virgl build <root@localhost>
Forwarded: not-needed
